# The released FPGA design that ./firmware-modern/fetch-pinned-xsa.sh downloads:
# the PlutoSky R2 design of this repository's release v0.1, built with Vivado
# 2022.2 from the tag (timing met, WNS +0.100 ns) and booted on an R2 on
# 2026-11-21. With it, everything but the FPGA design builds without Vivado.
#
# sha256 is of that release's system_top.xsa asset; fetch-pinned-xsa.sh refuses
# a mismatch. Changing it is a one-commit change HERE, after a release exists to
# point at. (The file keeps the name it has in the R1 repository, where the pin
# is a factory release's.)
tag=v0.1
sha256=5895090160704608f13524a4a8fabb0be355f7000182ef1c88aa6a7009c7668a
